Here's a JavaScript function that calculates the number of inversions (which is the minimum number of moves to sort the array):

```javascript
function countInversions(array) {
    let inversionCount = 0;

    for (let i = 0; i < array.length - 1; i++) {
        for (let j = i + 1; j < array.length; j++) {
